      "writtenOn": "2020-11-18T21:38:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I feel uncomfortable about this, especially without there being good reason. The connection between the size of the FsverityFormattedDigestSha256 array and the bytes being copied in doesn\u0027t have the type system checking that all bytes will be initialized. If it\u0027s a performance throttle then we can measure and justify it but clippy must be warning for a good reason. It\u0027s possible the compiler will work this out anyway or there is a more idiomatic way to construct this array that isn\u0027t coming to mind at the moment.",
      "revId": "69fc49f4a08c21f63760bcc5e8bdaf8abac7a720",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "26c83b65_7a3c84d5",
        "filename": "authfs/src/fsverity.rs",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 160,
      "author": {
        "id": 1042276
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-11-19T00:10:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If the compiler can optimize this, that\u0027ll be the best.  I don\u0027t think it\u0027ll be a bottleneck anyway, so changed to initialize with `[0u8; SIZE]` instead.",
      "parentUuid": "8d78d9ef_285760a8",
      "revId": "69fc49f4a08c21f63760bcc5e8bdaf8abac7a720",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
