        "id": 1139038
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-11-18T21:38:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is the desired behaviour even e.g. if the SHA hasher has an error? There are a few ways you can nest errors [1] but IDK what\u0027s the recommended practice.\n\n[1] -- https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/io/struct.Error.html#method.new",
      "revId": "69fc49f4a08c21f63760bcc5e8bdaf8abac7a720",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e29a87f7_488f0df9",
        "filename": "authfs/src/fsverity.rs",
