        "id": 1042276
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-11-19T00:10:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The user of this code will be a FUSE. EIO is the desired behavior when the content does not verify.  For hash error, it doesn\u0027t have to use EIO (but is what fs-verity currently does in kernel).  We can surely use a different EIO to provide better context, but I couldn\u0027t find any errno closes to \"hash error\" (and the OpenSSL/BoringSSL API doesn\u0027t seem to provide more visibility to the actual cause).",
      "parentUuid": "9bd33923_e5f83996",
      "revId": "69fc49f4a08c21f63760bcc5e8bdaf8abac7a720",
